rivals (at smallest declared effects) with cheap baseline / power_sweep / fiber_recouple tests;
the true out-of-catalog coupling shift was below the rule's grammar threshold on what was
measured; (ii) control cap 48: 26 vs 31 SUPPORTED (the shared count ended rival testing early).
B3 (frozen): "no effect" claims run exactly as B7; targeted tests have their own count (6).
dev1_*.log = B2, dev2_*.log = B3. B3: 0 SUPPORTED errors in every setting and cap.

## C. Design freeze
The commit that adds this section is the v1.5 design freeze F6: src/lab_brain/discovery_safety/v15/,
scripts/discovery_safety_v15_eval.py and scripts/discovery_safety_v14_eval.py are frozen as of F6.
The pre-registration (docs/reports/discovery-safety-v1.5-preregistration.md) was committed before.
Held-out seeds are derived from F6's full commit id only after F6 is pushed. The held-out
evaluation runs exactly once from F6.
